    docs(sync): re-pin the acceptance-plan census at a published tip — the block named a local commit
    
    The current-state block was pinned to `62dfeb0`, which the published ref does not contain:
    `git merge-base --is-ancestor 62dfeb0 origin/main` fails and
    `git ls-remote <published-url> | grep -c 62dfeb0` counts 0. It is a LOCAL commit,
    `board(pm): close CF-182` (2026-11-04 05:12:15 -0500), whose published twin is `f625a97` with the
    same subject — a sibling rebase re-landed it after the pin was written. The census' tip leg is
    `git cat-file -e "$tip:.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl"`, which resolves in the author's object
    store, so the same command was green where it was written and RED in every clone of the public
    repo: `DRIFT: acceptance plan names no resolvable tip`, exit 1 — at CF-099's own probe, a
    `complete` row whose acceptance command had stopped running. That is the class the block already
    names for its earlier `20f93ad` snapshot, one layer worse: there the numbers were unreproducible,
    here the pin itself was.
    
    Contradiction corrected in this commit. Measured at c5f7b2f from a clean clone of the published
    repo: 173 task rows, 340 events, 38 numbered sections, 41 arms, `SELFTEST: PASS` with 193 PASS
    rows and 50 fixture FAIL rows, `bash scripts/boardctl validate` -> `RESULT: OK (4 warning(s))`
    (CF-034 free-form, legacy duplicate event id 336, headerless board — all pre-existing). The block
    now names that tip and those numbers, states why the previous pin was unusable, and names the row
    that guards the recurrence.
    
    A repin alone does not stop it: any lane that measures at its own unpushed HEAD re-creates this
    (three lanes measured at local tips within the hour). CF-199 (pending, P3) owns the guard — resolve
    the pin against the PUBLISHED ref and make the arm fail on a locally present but unpublished sha.
    
    Board diff is insert-only: tasks.jsonl +1 line (CF-199, filed with a probe that was executed
    before it was written: `containment_refs=0 probe_rc=0`), events.jsonl +1 line (the writer's own
    task_created), docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md 1 insertion / 1 deletion.
    
    Board-and-docs-only commit, so the guard's Tier 1 lint skips when no implementation file is staged
    and it refuses this class with a DEGRADED PASS (repo precedent, CF-031). The disclosure is this
    paragraph; if the refusal fires the retry is `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit`.
    
